{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778378173017,"sessionID":"ses_1f067f91affenQPzTqXH6YPulT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_AWeaMW7Jn96w0cWLjJQzSQdl","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\n@@\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0001552))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0001649))\n+Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0001958))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0002491))\n@@\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0006005))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0006841))\n+Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0008187))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0008198))\n@@\n-AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15951842\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000743 \"Chondrocyte that is terminally differentiated, produces type X collagen, is large in size, and often associated with the replacement of cartilage by bone (endochondral ossification).\")\n-AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000743 \"is hypertrophic pathological or normal? and can it be described using a pato term?\")\n+AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25321476\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35179487\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41207902\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000743 \"A chondrocyte that is part of the hypertrophic cartilage zone. This cell is significantly enlarged and characterized by high expression of type X collagen (COL10A1) in both humans and mice. It actively coordinates endochondral ossification by mineralizing the extracellular matrix, attracting blood vessels via angiogenic signaling, and mediating the transition from cartilage to bone, often by transdifferentiating into an osteoblast rather than undergoing apoptosis.\")\n+AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000743 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3506>)\n+AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000743 \"Despite historical descriptions as 'terminally differentiated,' hypertrophic chondrocytes survive and transdifferentiate into osteoblasts. Genetic lineage tracing shows that hypertrophic chondrocytes do not simply undergo apoptosis but cross the cartilage-bone boundary, dedifferentiate into skeletal stem/progenitor cells, and then redifferentiate into osteoblasts and osteocytes. Single-cell RNA-seq further indicates that these chondrocyte-derived SSPCs are a major source of trabecular osteoblasts and marrow adipocytes. PMID:35179487 PMID:41207902\")\n AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000743 \"hypertrophic chondrocyte\")\n SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000743 obo:CL_0000138)\n+SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000743 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008187))\n+SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000743 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001958))\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\n@@ -3297,8 +3297,9 @@\n Declaration(Class(obo:CP_0000043))\n Declaration(Class(obo:D96882F1-8709-49AB-BCA9-772A67EA6C33))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0001552))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0001649))\n+Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0001958))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0002491))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0005903))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0005927))\n Declaration(Class(obo:GO_0005983))\n@@ -3467,8 +3468,9 @@\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0005382))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0005403))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0006005))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0006841))\n+Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0008187))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0008198))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0008304))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0008305))\n Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0008857))\n@@ -10180,12 +