{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778378219211,"sessionID":"ses_1f067f91affenQPzTqXH6YPulT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_WQ0831H9amtKiGiUB8qmQStx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated `hypertrophic chondrocyte` to remove the outdated terminal differentiation wording, added the requested UBERON and GO logical links, and found no existing `present in taxon Homo sapiens` axiom on this CL term to remove.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+## Summary\n+\n+Updated `CL_0000743` (`hypertrophic chondrocyte`) for issue #3506.\n+\n+## Changes\n+\n+- Replaced the outdated definition that described hypertrophic chondrocytes as terminally differentiated.\n+- Replaced the existing `rdfs:comment` with the requested lineage-tracing context about survival, dedifferentiation, and osteoblast/osteocyte contribution.\n+- Added the issue tracker annotation for issue #3506.\n+- Added declarations and subclass axioms linking the term to `UBERON:0008187` (`hypertrophic cartilage zone`) via `part_of` and `GO:0001958` (`endochondral ossification`) via `capable_of`.\n+- Checked for a `present in taxon Homo sapiens` axiom on `CL_0000743`; none was present in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The new definition and comment align the ontology entry with current evidence that hypertrophic chondrocytes are not simply terminal cells destined for apoptosis, but can contribute to skeletal stem/progenitor cells and osteoblast/osteocyte lineages. The added logical links mirror the revised textual definition by locating the cell in the hypertrophic cartilage zone and associating it with endochondral ossification.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Verified `CL_0000743` as the existing hypertrophic chondrocyte term.\n+- Verified `UBERON:0008187` as `hypertrophic cartilage zone` via OLS.\n+- Verified `GO:0001958` as `endochondral ossification` via OLS.\n+- Reviewed PubMed records for PMID:25321476, PMID:35179487, and PMID:41207902. The `aurelian` command requested by project guidance was unavailable in this environment.\n+- Validated functional syntax with `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-test.owl`.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated `hypertrophic chondrocyte` to remove the outdated terminal differentiation wording, added the requested UBERON and GO logical links, and found no existing `present in taxon Homo sapiens` axiom on this CL term to remove.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+## Summary\n+\n+Updated `CL_0000743` (`hypertrophic chondrocyte`) for issue #3506.\n+\n+## Changes\n+\n+- Replaced the outdated definition that described hypertrophic chondrocytes as terminally differentiated.\n+- Replaced the existing `rdfs:comment` with the requested lineage-tracing context about survival, dedifferentiation, and osteoblast/osteocyte contribution.\n+- Added the issue tracker annotation for issue #3506.\n+- Added declarations and subclass axioms linking the term to `UBERON:0008187` (`hypertrophic cartilage zone`) via `part_of` and `GO:0001958` (`endochondral ossification`) via `capable_of`.\n+- Checked for a `present in taxon Homo sapiens` axiom on `CL_0000743`; none was present in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The new definition and comment align the ontology entry with current evidence that hypertrophic chondrocytes are not simply terminal cells destined for apoptosis, but can contribute to skeletal stem/progenitor cells and osteoblast/osteocyte lineages. The added logical links mirror the revised textual definition by locating the cell in the hypertrophic cartilage zone and associating it with endochondral ossification.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Verified `CL_0000743` as the existing hypertrophic chondrocyte term.\n+- Verified `UBERON:0008187` as `hypertrophic cartilage zone` via OLS.\n+- Verified `GO:0001958` as `endochondral ossification` via OLS.\n+- Reviewed PubMed records for PMID:25321476, PMID:35179487, and PMID:41207902. The `aurelian` command requested by project guidance was unavailable in this environment.\n+- Validated functional syntax with `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-test.owl`.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","relativePath":"ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated `hypertrophic chondrocyte` to remove the outdated terminal differentiation wording, added the requested UBERON and GO logical links, and found no existing `present in taxon Homo sapiens` axiom on this CL term to remove.\n","additions":3,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md","relativePath":"PR_COMMENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-